## One thing outside my authority

`validate.sh --strict` on the bound packet `specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/013-addon-removal-and-speed-refinements` returns `RESULT: FAILED`, 3 errors:

- `PLACEHOLDER_FILLED`: 6 `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` placeholders in `implementation-summary.md` (lines 50, 61, 70, 81, 92, 101)
- `GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY`: `graph-metadata.json` `SOURCE_FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH`
- `GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT`: `description` and `causal_summary` in `description.json` drifted from fresh values

None of these are caused by this change. The fingerprint is re-derived over the packet's source docs, and every file I edited lives under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/`, so no path exists from these six edits to that metadata. The packet's own docs still carry scaffold placeholders and stale derived fields. Only the packet closer can repair them, with `repair-derived.cjs --apply` and by filling `implementation-summary.md`; both write files this brief does not name, so I left them alone. An `AC_COVERAGE` advisory (0/9 ACs cited) is reported as passing-but-under-floor for the same reason.
